  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The workflow was demonstrated and validated on a single historic monastery, which may not capture the full range of environmental and structural challenges found in other heritage sites.",
      "what": "This study presents a reproducible multi-sensor workflow that integrates UAV and close-range photogrammetry, SLAM-based mapping, and geodetic control within a single reference system to document complex cultural heritage monuments. Tested on a historic monastery, both photogrammetry and SLAM datasets achieved centimeter-level agreement with geodetic observations, with photogrammetry providing superior exterior coverage and textures, while SLAM captured interior spaces rapidly.",
      "why": "It establishes a reliable, integrated methodology that overcomes the individual limitations of photogrammetry and SLAM, providing a complete and metrically accurate 3D representation of complex structures for conservation and monitoring."
    }
